# user.md — operator & agent identity (copy to user.md, fill in, gitignore the real file)

No PII or secrets in this template. The real `user.md` is gitignored, same as YC's `recruit-config/user.md`.

## Agent identity

- **Agent name:** {AgentName} — pick something short, warm, obviously not a human name pretending to be human.
- **Agent mailbox:** recruiting@otpless.com
- **Disclosure signature** (every candidate-facing email/WhatsApp message ends with this, non-negotiable):
  ```
  — {AgentName}, OTPLESS's recruiting agent (AI), working with Satyam
  ```
- **Agent Slack handle:** @{AgentName} (posts in #hiring as itself once qm/P2 is live)
- **Agent Notion user:** {machine user name} (every tracker edit attributed to the agent)

## Operators

| Operator | Role | Owns | Email |
|---|---|---|---|
| Satyam | Founder | Founding Recruiter, Security, ML pipelines; **all offers/comp/closes across every role** | {founder email} |
| {CTO name} | CTO | Technical pipelines — Android SDK, iOS SDK, Backend, AI Automation; work-sample review | {cto email} |

Founding Recruiter (once hired) inherits the whole system by editing this file — no code changes.

## Logistics

- **Meet link:** {meet/zoom link}
- **Office address:** {Bangalore office address placeholder}
- **Slack channel:** #hiring
- **Timezone:** Asia/Kolkata (IST) — always schedule and display times in IST.
- **Default scheduling blocks:** Tuesday & Thursday, 5:00–7:00pm IST (intro calls + technical rounds back-to-back within the block; ask the operator before using any other block).

## Candidate channel preference

WhatsApp > email. WhatsApp Business API is not yet wired (Phase 3) — until it lands, the agent drafts the WhatsApp message text in-session and a human copies/pastes it manually. Same draft-first approval gate applies to WhatsApp text as to email.

